;; The network (doc/go/BOX-NOTES.md, S5; guest/abi's NetInfo and the rest):
;; TCP streams the monitor makes on the guest's behalf, under a NetPolicy.
;; The guest names its sockets by handles; nothing it asks blocks its vCPU:
;; a connection's bytes are read into a buffer of the monitor's by a
;; goroutine of its own and written from another, a listener's connections
;; accepted by a third, a dial and a name's lookup made by one each, and the
;; guest's calls take what is there or answer EAGAIN.  Every change a guest
;; might wait for adds one to a count (NetEvents), which the guest polls
;; while it waits, as it polls the console.



